{"uid":"e5faa8a6f4dd0a6b","name":"test_follow_pretty_tail_shows_backlog_live_then_keeps_streaming","fullName":"tests.test_cli_logs_follow_liveness#test_follow_pretty_tail_shows_backlog_live_then_keeps_streaming","historyId":"b8a15c96c23ab311cfd1dee50269bb92","time":{"start":1791867520196,"stop":1791867523733,"duration":3537},"description":"Genuine liveness proof for the follow+tail combo: once the job has\n    already produced more than N rendered lines, spawn `-Nf`, confirm the\n    first line arrives while the job is still running (not buffered until\n    job end -- same liveness bar as task 056), then let the job finish and\n    confirm the total output grew PAST the initial N-line backlog once\n    more content arrived live (proving `-Nf` doesn't just stop at N and\n    exit -- it shows N lines of backlog, then keeps following).\n\n    task 010 (B.4): STUB_HOLD_FILE/STUB_HOLD_PHASE=\"worker\" holds the\n    first worker iteration open (mid-preamble) instead of racing a real\n    STUB_SLEEP window to catch the job with backlog already produced but\n    not yet terminal -- a held first iteration's own rich-event preamble\n    (planning + partial worker transcript) already exceeds the smaller\n    `tail_n` used here (confirmed: 6 lines while held vs 3 threshold),\n    so no further real wait is needed before spawning `-Nf`.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Genuine liveness proof for the follow+tail combo: once the job has<br />\nalready produced more than N rendered lines, spawn <code>-Nf</code>, confirm the<br />\nfirst line arrives while the job is still running (not buffered until<br />\njob end -- same liveness bar as task 056), then let the job finish and<br />\nconfirm the total output grew PAST the initial N-line backlog once<br />\nmore content arrived live (proving <code>-Nf</code> doesn't just stop at N and<br />\nexit -- it shows N lines of backlog, then keeps following).</p>\n<pre><code>task 010 (B.4): STUB_HOLD_FILE/STUB_HOLD_PHASE=&quot;worker&quot; holds the\n